{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304892-artifact-that-enhances-sorcery","id":1304892,"title":"Artifact that enhances sorcery?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-14T15:22:03-07:00","id":1304892,"title":"Artifact that enhances sorcery?","content":"I have a player that wants to make an artifact that enhances sorcerous workings. He wants the base power before evocations to lower the time it takes for the duration per roll.<br /> <br /> So, given this, say the artifact lowers the base time from one week to 3 days. What level would that be? I'm thinking 4 or 5. Further thoughts on evocations to enhance sorcery are welcome. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm not sure where to start.<br /> <br /> Edit: Given new info:<br /> <br /> <b>I think having the artifact reduce the time needed for a terrestrial level working first as the base effect is the right way to go. Then the evocations to reduce the time needed for celestial &amp; solar workings require the PC to learn those levels of sorcery as a prerequisite.<br /> <br /> The question still remains though, what level of artifact should this be?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2783,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","user":"Tytalus","date":". 04-14-2019, 11:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T16:14:47-07:00","id":1304906,"title":"","content":"I think that the base time for Sorcery should not be adjusted. It would be better instead to have an artifact that reduced the difficult of workings or an artifact that gave bonus dice when doing a working. I would suggest that an artifact that reduce the difficulty by one would be level 3, two would be level 4, and four would be level 5. Since the difficulty would be reduced, the overall time would be reduced.<br /> <br /> As for Evocations, they would probably relate to giving bonus dice or bonus means to the creation of sorcerous workings. More advanced Evocations might even allow sorcerers to expend crafting experience instead of normal experience for sorcerous workings or may allow sorcerers to function at a higher initiation level for the purpose of creating sorcerous workings. The capstone Evocation may allow a sorcerer to create temporary sorcerous workings, which would last for one scene, by spending a turn per roll and by spending motes of Essence and Willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25244-the-fool-of-creation","name":"The Fool of Creation","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T16:35:52-07:00","id":1304915,"title":"","content":"An artifact that enhances sorerous workings would definitely be N/A. That's speeding up fundamentally enhancing the universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T16:54:19-07:00","id":1304919,"title":"","content":"<br /> I would think Raski's book would count as this no?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ah probably not, didn't read what you said in specifics<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":3742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","user":"Iceblade44","date":". 04-14-2019, 08:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T17:14:54-07:00","id":1304921,"title":"","content":"There are Artifacts in the setting that do this stuff. The Book of Three Circles, the Emerald Thurible, etc. I don't know of one that isn't N/A. I'd consider going with a Hearthstone or even a Manse for this kind of ability, but that's just details.<br /> <br /> Thematically, I think most Sorcery enhancement should come with some kind of cost. Not necessarily a Monkey's Paw &quot;Oh no, my Hubris&quot; thing, but some kind of drawback or investment. Both the Thurible and the Book have these, though more in terms of NPC drawbacks than PCs (The Thurible can summon 2nd circle demons but doesn't guarantee Mnemon can bind them, and the Book has fed Raksi's obsession over centuries)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T17:59:59-07:00","id":1304930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304892-artifact-that-enhances-sorcery?p=1304915#post1304915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">fundamentally enhancing the universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>What happened to it being just breeding new mundane life forms?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T18:07:15-07:00","id":1304932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maseiken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304892-artifact-that-enhances-sorcery?p=1304921#post1304921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are Artifacts in the setting that do this stuff. The Book of Three Circles, the Emerald Thurible, etc. I don't know of one that isn't N/A.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where are you getting that about either of them?<br /> <br /> The Emerald Thurible in particular. That thing was always about summoning demons. Come What Fire Has Wrought, you've got an Artifact that grants the spell to summon Second Circles, can make it cheaper for demons to materialize, and doubles 9s for some rolls related to demons.<br /> <br /> What about that says N/A?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T18:27:44-07:00","id":1304935,"title":"","content":"The difficulty here is that nothing currently printed in 3e lets you reduce the time needed to perform a Working, nor is there anything that breaks the dice cap for Workings so there\u2019s currently no reference to use to figure out how to balance such an effect.<br /> <br /> That said, I would say the main things to keep in mind is that Solar level workings should remain epic feats that take lots of time to perform and that you never let minor workings become so easy that they become the first solution to every problem. Make sure you enforce the xp costs of Workings.<br /> <br /> If I was going to do something like that, I'd create an Evocation that had Celestial Circle Sorcery as a prereq and allow you to reduce the Means available to your Terrestrial Workings at a rate of one Means per 2 days, minimum one day. So, if you spend one means, you get to roll after 5 days instead of 7 and spending 3 means would turn your interval into a day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T18:28:52-07:00","id":1304936,"title":"","content":"Also, there are a couple of artifacts in Arms of the chosen that mess with Sorcery, neither of them are N/A","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T18:30:00-07:00","id":1304937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304892-artifact-that-enhances-sorcery?p=1304930#post1304930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What happened to it being just breeding new mundane life forms?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean it's not just that. The power of it at baseline isn't remotely the same as it is at celestial or solar workings. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304892-artifact-that-enhances-sorcery?p=1304930#post1304930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where are you getting that about either of them?<br /> <br /> The Emerald Thurible in particular. That thing was always about summoning demons. Come What Fire Has Wrought, you've got an Artifact that grants the spell to summon Second Circles, can make it cheaper for demons to materialize, and doubles 9s for some rolls related to demons.<br /> <br /> What about that says N/A?</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that it lets you summon demons higher than your ability. Last I checked if a lunar or sidereal had that they could summon third circle demons. The book of three circles has also always been N/A because it's a powerful artifact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T19:13:13-07:00","id":1304947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304892-artifact-that-enhances-sorcery?p=1304935#post1304935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difficulty here is that nothing currently printed in 3e lets you reduce the time needed to perform a Working, nor is there anything that breaks the dice cap for Workings so there\u2019s currently no reference to use to figure out how to balance such an effect.<br /> <br /> That said, I would say the main things to keep in mind is that Solar level workings should remain epic feats that take lots of time to perform and that you never let minor workings become so easy that they become the first solution to every problem. Make sure you enforce the xp costs of Workings.<br /> <br /> If I was going to do something like that, I'd create an Evocation that had Celestial Circle Sorcery as a prereq and allow you to reduce the Means available to your Terrestrial Workings at a rate of one Means per 2 days, minimum one day. So, if you spend one means, you get to roll after 5 days instead of 7 and spending 3 means would turn your interval into a day.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This gives me something to work with, thank you!<br /> <br /> <u><b>I think having the artifact reduce the time needed for a terrestrial level working first as the base effect is the right way to go. Then the evocations to reduce the time needed for celestial &amp; solar workings require the PC to learn those levels of sorcery as a prerequisite.<br /> <br /> The question still remains though, what level of artifact should this be?</b></u>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2783,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","user":"Tytalus","date":". 04-14-2019, 11:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T19:13:22-07:00","id":1304948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304892-artifact-that-enhances-sorcery?p=1304937#post1304937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean it's not just that. The power of it at baseline isn't remotely the same as it is at celestial or solar workings.</div> </div> </div> </div>What in either of those is enhancing the universe?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that it lets you summon demons higher than your ability. Last I checked if a lunar or sidereal had that they could summon third circle demons. The book of three circles has also always been N/A because it's a powerful artifact.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll grant that in the milieu of First and Second Edition, the power of the Emerald Thurible might qualify for N/A insofar as it's significantly higher than what we got from Artifact 5, which spoke to how absolutely goddamn pitiful Artifact 5 was in those Editions.<br /> <br /> I mean, very few Artifacts were anything to write home about, but 5 was the one in particular that had a real dissonance between how it was described in rules and fiction and what the published examples could do.<br /> <br /> And so, any time you had an Artifact that was halfway interesting, it had to be set to N/A, because it didn't really fit at 5 when the baseline was the freaking Daiklave of Conquest.<br /> <br /> But now we have an Edition in which Artifact 5 is worth a damn, and the powers of the Emerald Thurible and Book of Three Circles to be found in the write-ups of Mnemon and Raksi respectively are no higher than it. They certainly don't reach the levels that Arms of the Chosen infers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T19:17:16-07:00","id":1304950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304892-artifact-that-enhances-sorcery?p=1304948#post1304948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What in either of those is enhancing the universe?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'll grant that in the milieu of First and Second Edition, the power of the Emerald Thurible might qualify for N/A insofar as it's significantly higher than what we got from Artifact 5, which spoke to how absolutely goddamn pitiful Artifact 5 was in those Editions.<br /> <br /> I mean, very few Artifacts were anything to write home about, but 5 was the one in particular that had a real dissonance between how it was described in rules and fiction and what the published examples could do.<br /> <br /> And so, any time you had an Artifact that was halfway interesting, it had to be set to N/A, because it didn't really fit at 5 when the baseline was the freaking Daiklave of Conquest.<br /> <br /> But now we have an Edition in which Artifact 5 is worth a damn, and the powers of the Emerald Thurible and Book of Three Circles to be found in the write-ups of Mnemon and Raksi respectively are no higher than it. They certainly don't reach the levels that Arms of the Chosen infers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solar workings can fundimentally alter creation. This isn't trival. Also, i don't think you realize how much a third circle demon is much much more powerful than any artifact in currently stated. 3rd circle demons are much more capable of moving and shaking to world compared to any artifact currently in the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> Both artifacts let them utilize spells beyond them. A dragon blooded outside of that one artifact and another n/a artifact cannot summon a 2nd circle demon. Raksi with the book can cast spells she doesn't know as well as capture them for later use. These are world shaking artifacts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-14-2019, 10:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T19:55:38-07:00","id":1304959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304892-artifact-that-enhances-sorcery?p=1304950#post1304950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Solar workings can fundimentally alter creation. This isn't trival.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not trivial, but it's also at the very top of the scale, so measuring what can be done to workings as a whole by that isn't really sensible.<br /> <br /> Also, it's kind of trivial. Universal metaphysical alterations are said to be &quot;subtle&quot;. Things the likes of which most people will tangibly experience can't be bigger than a city.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, i don't think you realize how much a third circle demon is much much more powerful than any artifact in currently stated. 3rd circle demons are much more capable of moving and shaking to world compared to any artifact currently in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't realize it because this Edition has not yet published a Third Circle Demon to measure its powers against Artifacts.<br /> <br /> Also, this doesn't really feel true to Third Circle Demons that have existed in the game thus far.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both artifacts let them utilize spells beyond them. A dragon blooded outside of that one artifact cannot summon a 2nd circle demon. Raksi with the book can cast spells she doesn't know as well as capture them for later use. These are world shaking artifacts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Artifact 5 is pretty world shaking. We've also got a level 5 soulsteel axe from which people can learn spells.<br /> <br /> Being able to perform magic that you couldn't do without them seems rather the point of Artifacts. A Solar with Gnomon can fuck around with time and grow peaches of immortality in less than 500 years, and it is not N/A.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the Emerald Thurible might be closer to Artifact 4 right now.<br /> <br /> I'm reminded of Irenio's Bell, a Thunderbolt Shield that can summon First Circle Demons, just as an example of an Artifact intrinsically having demon-summoning power. The Emerald Thurible seems rather different with how its whole deal is summoning demons, so it leans more into that subject.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T19:59:37-07:00","id":1304961,"title":"","content":"What dice caps exist with Sorcery? Exalted should be able to use their Excellencies with Sorcery without any trouble, correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25244-the-fool-of-creation","name":"The Fool of Creation","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T20:40:08-07:00","id":1304970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304892-artifact-that-enhances-sorcery?p=1304959#post1304959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not trivial, but it's also at the very top of the scale, so measuring what can be done to workings as a whole by that isn't really sensible.<br /> <br /> Also, it's kind of trivial. Universal metaphysical alterations are said to be &quot;subtle&quot;. Things the likes of which most people will tangibly experience can't be bigger than a city.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speeding those things up considerably is still innately altering the fundimental of those styles. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> I don't realize it because this Edition has not yet published a Third Circle Demon to measure its powers against Artifacts.<br /> <br /> Also, this doesn't really feel true to Third Circle Demons that have existed in the game thus far. </div> </div> </div>We have 2nd circle demons and they feel much more powerful than any dragon blooded. Memnon basically has bodyguards that are stronger than anything else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Artifact 5 is pretty world shaking. We've also got a level 5 soulsteel axe from which people can learn spells.<br /> <br /> Being able to perform magic that you couldn't do without them seems rather the point of Artifacts. A Solar with Gnomon can fuck around with time and grow peaches of immortality in less than 500 years, and it is not N/A.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the Emerald Thurible might be closer to Artifact 4 right now.<br /> <br /> I'm reminded of Irenio's Bell, a Thunderbolt Shield that can summon First Circle Demons, just as an example of an Artifact intrinsically having demon-summoning power. The Emerald Thurible seems rather different with how its whole deal is summoning demons, so it leans more into that subject. </div> </div> </div>First circle demons are jokes compared to something that can a second circle can. There's no way you can justify a dragon blooded being able to cast celestial sorcery as being anything else less than N/A.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T21:28:46-07:00","id":1304982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304892-artifact-that-enhances-sorcery?p=1304970#post1304970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speeding those things up considerably is still innately altering the fundimental of those styles.</div> </div> </div> </div>What?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">We have 2nd circle demons and they feel much more powerful than any dragon blooded. Memnon basically has bodyguards that are stronger than anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the benefit of Artifact 5.<br /> <br /> Stormcaller is more powerful than any given Dragon Blooded as well (even if their Evocations would probably have to go a different path following Sleeping Devil, Wake), so what does that tell you?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">First circle demons are jokes compared to something that can a second circle can.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why you need something higher than Artifact 3 to summon the latter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no way you can justify a dragon blooded being able to cast celestial sorcery as being anything else less than N/A.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd start by pointing out how one Evocation that is equivalent to one spell is not that.<br /> <br /> I'd also propose that being able to summon a Second Circle Demon is something that you need at least Essence 4 to do, if not 5. It's not as if it should yield that power to every Terrestrial who attunes to it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T21:31:39-07:00","id":1304984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304892-artifact-that-enhances-sorcery?p=1304982#post1304982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd also propose that being able to summon a Second Circle Demon is something that you need at least Essence 4 to do, if not 5. It's not as if it should yield that power to every Terrestrial who attunes to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what the artifact does. Evocations change but that's it's innate ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T21:37:03-07:00","id":1304987,"title":"","content":"An N/A artifact should be something as powerful as the Mantle of Brigid (+5 Essence and upgrades the sorcery potential of its ownership), the Eye of Autochthon (rewrite reality), or a Skywolf (flying cruisers). Just giving Terrestrial Exalted the ability to cast a single Celestial Spell should be a level 4 artifact (the artifact used by Mnemon is level 5 because it gives three spells, First Circle to mortals, Second Circle to DBs, and Third Circle to Celestial Exalted, and gives an alternative methods for paying for demon summoning).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25244-the-fool-of-creation","name":"The Fool of Creation","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T21:40:46-07:00","id":1304988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Fool of Creation</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304892-artifact-that-enhances-sorcery?p=1304987#post1304987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An N/A artifact should be something as powerful as the Mantle of Brigid (+5 Essence and upgrades the sorcery potential of its ownership), the Eye of Autochthon (rewrite reality), or a Skywolf (flying cruisers). Just giving Terrestrial Exalted the ability to cast a single Celestial Spell should be a level 4 artifact (the artifact used by Mnemon is level 5 because it gives three spells, First Circle to mortals, Second Circle to DBs, and Third Circle to Celestial Exalted, and gives an alternative methods for paying for demon summoning).</div> </div> </div> </div>Vance gave it 5. The book of three circles would still be N/A. Not all N/A artifacts are the same. An artifact that augments sorcerous workings are much more powerful than a single spell though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T21:59:21-07:00","id":1304990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304892-artifact-that-enhances-sorcery?p=1304988#post1304988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vance gave it 5. The book of three circles would still be N/A. Not all N/A artifacts are the same. An artifact that augments sorcerous workings are much more powerful than a single spell though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Source on that? Not to be snarky, but honestly curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T22:16:02-07:00","id":1304991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304892-artifact-that-enhances-sorcery?p=1304990#post1304990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Source on that? Not to be snarky, but honestly curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>He did it just a few minutes ago. I actually think older editions gave it 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T22:45:03-07:00","id":1304994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304892-artifact-that-enhances-sorcery?p=1304991#post1304991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He did it just a few minutes ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am so confused.... Where? I didn't see such a thing in this thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304892-artifact-that-enhances-sorcery?p=1304991#post1304991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually think older editions gave it 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it was an N/A artifact in older editions. I think it was mentioned in 2E, but not given dots, except as a grave good? (B&amp;W)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T23:08:09-07:00","id":1304998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304892-artifact-that-enhances-sorcery?p=1304994#post1304994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am so confused.... Where? I didn't see such a thing in this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ask the devs thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T23:57:32-07:00","id":1305002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304892-artifact-that-enhances-sorcery?p=1304932#post1304932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Snip about Thurible/B3S*<br /> <br /> What about that says N/A?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're actually completely right. Thurible was N/A in 2nd Ed, which is what I was going by but that's not at all a reliable gauge. Misstep on my part.<br /> <br /> Back on topic, given that the artefact doesn't let you do anything you can't already do, I don't think it's necessarily automatically a 5 or even a 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","user":"Maseiken","date":". 04-15-2019, 03:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-15T03:44:09-07:00","id":1305013,"title":"","content":"I think enhancing sorcerous workings is a viable but such an artifact should impose its own themes and caveats upon the projects.<br /> <br /> For example, the Scarred By Nightmares sorcerous initiation has a merit that absolves you of the xp cost for sorcerous workings that never leave the wyld. I could easily see an artifact enhancing workings in a similar capacity where there's thematic limitations being set upon your creations or a unhealthy dependency where its loss or destruction ends every working it enhanced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-15T04:14:35-07:00","id":1305015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304892-artifact-that-enhances-sorcery?p=1305013#post1305013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think enhancing sorcerous workings is a viable but such an artifact should impose its own themes and caveats upon the projects.<br /> <br /> For example, the Scarred By Nightmares sorcerous initiation has a merit that absolves you of the xp cost for sorcerous workings that never leave the wyld. I could easily see an artifact enhancing workings in a similar capacity where there's thematic limitations being set upon your creations or a unhealthy dependency where its loss or destruction ends every working it enhanced.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember something. Conan the barbarian rpg. Ring of set. <br /> <br /> Pretty nice. Gives good bonuses to magic and power. <br /> <br /> And if you ever lose it? You're fucked. Putting on the ring means that if you ever lose it, you lose any xp you obtained after putting it on. You get good powers... At the cost of making it so that you can never lose it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-15T04:33:07-07:00","id":1305016,"title":"","content":"I can see some Artifacts that count as a method, granting additional intervals (die rolls) to sorcerous workings. Not so much speeding them up though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-15T05:14:23-07:00","id":1305019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304892-artifact-that-enhances-sorcery?p=1305016#post1305016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see some Artifacts that count as a method, granting additional intervals (die rolls) to sorcerous workings. Not so much speeding them up though.</div> </div> </div> </div>.... I just have a headcanon that you can reduce the interval, as long as you're willing to reduce the total number of intervals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-15T06:27:35-07:00","id":1305028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Fool of Creation</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304892-artifact-that-enhances-sorcery?p=1304961#post1304961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What dice caps exist with Sorcery? Exalted should be able to use their Excellencies with Sorcery without any trouble, correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the standard dice caps apply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-15T07:21:20-07:00","id":1305037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304892-artifact-that-enhances-sorcery?p=1305019#post1305019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> .... I just have a headcanon that you can reduce the interval, as long as you're willing to reduce the total number of intervals.</div> </div> </div> </div>That...is much more balanced than what I saw. Sorry","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-15T07:28:53-07:00","id":1305041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304892-artifact-that-enhances-sorcery?p=1305037#post1305037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That...is much more balanced than what I saw. Sorry</div> </div> </div> </div>... I'm curious. <br /> <br /> What did you see?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-15T08:00:43-07:00","id":1305050,"title":"","content":"I find the idea of Artifacts that can enhance workings while narrowing them to be compelling.<br /> <br /> I do wonder if any Artifact should be able to interact with sorcery in this manner that isn't a relic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304892-artifact-that-enhances-sorcery?p=1304984#post1304984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That's what the artifact does. Evocations change but that's it's innate ability.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It was when Artifacts were simpler things, but there's a question of whether or not that's a bit too powerful to access as the default.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'm not saying it strictly has to be, but that it's worth exploring.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-15T08:11:02-07:00","id":1305055,"title":"","content":"Now I'm inspired.<br /> <br /> I want to write an artifact. Mortal accessible. Focus on golems, minions and monsters. Get reduced difficulty and ambition for doing things like making golems, inflicting mutations, or making monsters. <br /> <br /> Evocation that let you summon extra elementals or demons, or let you give them extra power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-15T12:51:33-07:00","id":1305108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304892-artifact-that-enhances-sorcery?p=1304982#post1304982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why you need something higher than Artifact 3 to summon the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically Irenio's Bell can do so with an Essence 4 repurchase of the capstone Evocation. So it's not out of bounds for Artifact 3, though likely at the very limit of what one can do and requiring a powerful user who's mastered its Evocations.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T10:43:39-07:00","id":1305760,"title":"","content":"So I've decided to rate my artifact as level 3. It will reduce time for Terrestrial workings by one interval as a base power. Evocations will reduce the interval for celestial and solar as the sorceror learns those levels of sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T20:12:19-07:00","id":1305886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304892-artifact-that-enhances-sorcery?p=1305760#post1305760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I've decided to rate my artifact as level 3. It will reduce time for Terrestrial workings by one interval as a base power. Evocations will reduce the interval for celestial and solar as the sorceror learns those levels of sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about another evocation to reduce difficulty?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T09:16:28-07:00","id":1306014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304892-artifact-that-enhances-sorcery?p=1305886#post1305886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about another evocation to reduce difficulty?</div> </div> </div> </div>As in, lowering the difficulty of the finess rolls, or ambition? That's a possibility I hadn't thought of and a good suggestion. By how much do you think is reasonable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T09:44:54-07:00","id":1306026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tytalus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304892-artifact-that-enhances-sorcery?p=1306014#post1306014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As in, lowering the difficulty of the finess rolls, or ambition? That's a possibility I hadn't thought of and a good suggestion. By how much do you think is reasonable?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lowering the difficulty. <br /> <br /> I once had an idea. An evocation that works to give you decreased difficulty and extra rolls... As long as you hew to a certain theme in your work. <br /> <br /> Want to make a waterfall in the desert? Nope, no easy stuff. You gotta make a machine that when cranked, spews out water. Want to make a golem? It's gotta be a steam and diesel punk, with gears, rods, pipes, and other shit. Wanna throw death Ray? You don't fire it from your hands. You conjure a Ray gun and then start firing. <br /> <br /> Our sorcerer has access to spells similar to alchemical protocols and sorcery. She's going to make like a Agatha Heterdoyne.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T11:35:26-07:00","id":1306054,"title":"","content":"Reducing the interval by one is really powerful, that potentially allows a Terrestrial 1 to occur instantly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25244-the-fool-of-creation","name":"The Fool of Creation","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T11:46:11-07:00","id":1306058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Fool of Creation</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304892-artifact-that-enhances-sorcery?p=1306054#post1306054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reducing the interval by one is really powerful, that potentially allows a Terrestrial 1 to occur instantly.</div> </div> </div> </div>... I still think the rule for letting you reduce intervals in exchange for reducing total number of intervals is a good idea.<br /> <br /> You don't need to spend entire weeks just to ward pests from a field. Just cut down the intervals from 5 to 2, from once a week to once every hours, then bam. One ward cast. Just make sure to max out stats and spend an excellency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T12:15:48-07:00","id":1306063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Fool of Creation</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304892-artifact-that-enhances-sorcery?p=1306054#post1306054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reducing the interval by one is really powerful, that potentially allows a Terrestrial 1 to occur instantly.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would still take 3 days, and cost the usual XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}